    "body": "We've used quotations elsewhere (e.g. [\"geolocation\"](https://www.w3.org/TR/geolocation/#dfn-geolocation))... but it's not mandatory. However, I think permission names are always used as opaque strings. About code, I guess it can just be wrapped? \r\n\r\nSo:\r\n```suggestion\r\n<a for=\"powerful feature\">name</a> <code>\"<dfn export permission>notifications</dfn>\"</code>. [[!Permissions]]\r\n```",
    "created_at": "2022-10-04T06:00:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-04T06:00:25Z",
